studio/.migrate-cache.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Photographs and source media do NOT live in git.
#
# Two reasons, and both are hard limits rather than preferences. GitHub rejects
# any single file over 100 MB, and the Nelly House drone footage runs to 511 MB
# a file — the whole reference folder is 3.7 GB. And the implementation contract
# forbids committing photographs at all: the Nelly House images are Condé Nast's
# and are licensed to btl, not to a public code host.
#
# The photographs' real home is Sanity, which is the entire point of putting a
# CMS in. The untouched originals need their own backup — Drive, or the
# practice's own storage — because git is not a photo archive and should not be
# asked to be one.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
references and inspirations/
projects/

# The site's OWN assets must be tracked, or a fresh clone builds a site with no
# logo and no opening film — which is exactly what Netlify does on every deploy.
#
# So the rule is drawn by PATH, not by extension. The two folders above hold the
# camera originals — 3.7 GB, single drone files over 500 MB — and neither ships.
# What remains under web/public is the logo, the typeface and one script: the
# handful of files that are genuinely part of the code rather than the content.
#
# The photographs and the opening film both live in the CMS now, which is why
# there is no longer a video folder here at all. An earlier version of this file
# excluded *.MP4, and on a case-insensitive filesystem that also swallowed the
# transcoded .mp4 the homepage opened with — so the deploy would have built a
# site with no film in it.

# packaged copies — rebuildable, and one holds the photographs inline
*.zip
btl-projects.html
_claude-design-upload/

# os
.DS_Store
